.TH ferry 1  Ferry "Ferry Manual"
.SH NAME
ferry \- Ferry – secure P2P file sharing over QUIC, without a cloud or mDNS
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBferry\fR [\fB\-\-lang\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Ferry – secure P2P file sharing over QUIC, without a cloud or mDNS
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-lang\fR \fI<CODE>\fR
Interface language for this run (`en`, `pl`); overrides the saved setting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ferry\-send(1)
Send files and folders to a trusted or nearby device (`\-\-to`), or share one file by a one\-time TICKET
.TP
ferry\-localsend(1)
Send files to LocalSend apps (iPhone, iPad, Mac, …) and find them on the local network
.TP
ferry\-integrate(1)
Add "Send with Ferry" to the file managers of this user (Dolphin, Nautilus, Nemo; Linux)
.TP
ferry\-history(1)
Show finished transfers, newest first, or search them
.TP
ferry\-web(1)
Share files with a web browser on the local network and receive files from it, through a one\-time link and QR code (the other device needs no app)
.TP
ferry\-text(1)
Send text or a link; the receiver copies it to the clipboard after accepting
.TP
ferry\-receive(1)
Download a file shared by TICKET
.TP
ferry\-daemon(1)
Run in the background; trusted devices with Auto\-Accept are accepted automatically
.TP
ferry\-tui(1)
Interactive terminal user interface
.TP
ferry\-ticket(1)
Show this device\*(Aqs TICKET (text and QR code) for pairing
.TP
ferry\-discover(1)
Search for Ferry devices on the local network (own UDP broadcast, no mDNS)
.TP
ferry\-pair(1)
Pair with a nearby device (name or Node ID from `ferry discover`); the other side confirms and both show the same code
.TP
ferry\-pairing(1)
Let unknown devices send pairing requests for a few minutes, although `paired\-only` is on (also for a running daemon or TUI); `\-\-close` ends it
.TP
ferry\-guide(1)
Short answers to the usual questions: sending, pairing, devices without Ferry, iPhone and Mac, local or internet, devices that do not show up, privacy
.TP
ferry\-name(1)
Show or change the name of this device visible to others
.TP
ferry\-language(1)
Show or change the interface language (`en`, `pl`)
.TP
ferry\-network(1)
Show or change the network mode: `local` (no external servers, default), `internet` (also through the free public iroh relays, for devices in different networks), `relay` (also through your own relays) or `relay\-only` (only through your own relays, never directly)
.TP
ferry\-peer(1)
Manage trusted devices
.TP
ferry\-config(1)
Show or change settings (`ferry config list`, `get`, `set`, `unset`, `path`)
.TP
ferry\-identity(1)
Show, back up or restore this device\*(Aqs identity (its Node ID key)
.TP
ferry\-doctor(1)
Network and configuration diagnostics
.TP
ferry\-completions(1)
Print the shell completion script, e.g. `ferry completions bash > ~/.local/share/bash\-completion/completions/ferry` (packages install it already)
.SH EXTRA
New to Ferry? `ferry guide` explains the first steps in a few lines.
